# Real, disclosed gap closed here (CRITICAL-tier review, `DEC-160`):
# `gcloud builds submit` resolves `.gcloudignore` -- falling back to
# `.gitignore` only if this file is absent -- relative to the SOURCE
# directory it's given, never the repo root and never `.dockerignore`.
# Every manual deploy in this project's history (`DEC-098` through
# `DEC-159`) has run `gcloud builds submit` from inside `backend/`
# directly, with no file here to consult -- the repo root's own real
# `.gitignore` (which does list `backend/.env`) was never actually
# read for this specific operation, since a `.gcloudignore`/`.gitignore`
# lookup relative to `backend/` looks for `backend/.gitignore`, which
# has never existed. This file closes that gap directly, permanently,
# for every future `gcloud builds submit` run from this directory --
# CI's own build (`ci.yml`'s `deploy` job) was never actually at risk
# (a real GitHub Actions checkout only ever has committed files on
# disk to begin with), but every real manual deploy before this fix
# genuinely could have uploaded `backend/.env`'s real contents into the
# Cloud Build staging bucket's build-context tarball.
.env
.env.*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
tests/
.git/
